{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1528028-ascension","id":1528028,"title":"Ascension","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-01-05T08:59:25-08:00","id":1528028,"title":"Ascension","content":"I know it usually gets talked about only in terms or Archmastery, infact I entirely missed that sleepers can ascend directl? (Or more likely awakened mages).<br /> <br /> But something else got me thinking about it earlier, and I want to know what ascension project you would want to be your legacy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Mages know the legends of Ascension, where mortals become Supernal Forms. </div> </div> </div><br /> * The spark was reading about dedicated magical tool, how your are supposed to find something which maybe reflects a portion of your Nimbus and then synchronize it with your soul.<br /> <br /> The idea of the Nimbus as a part of your true Supernal self (as exemplified by the enraputed being losing their wisdom and having the Supernal directly manifest from their Nimbus, like usually this is contained by a Mage's wisdom, but Greater Tupla - aka a type of Supernal being - simply errupt from your Nimbus if you don't act out your fault), and you Dedicated magical tool being an aspect of the fallen world which reflects some part of the true Supernal self.<br /> <br /> Contrasted with creating a soulstone, where you impose your Supernal self - imprint your Nimbus - upon the fallen. Dedicating a magical tool aligns your soul more with the fallen world (or located a part of the fallen which aligns withyour Supernal self) - see also shadow names.<br /> <br /> It feels like there is a great alignment which is requires for Ascension. That the act dedication of a magical tool or creating/adopting a shadow name is a mere child's play compared to altering the Fallen sufficiently to ascend. Aligning your soul with something bigger which makes your soul fit into some Supernal truth.<br /> <br /> I guess the take depends on whether you feel As Below, So Above, is more valid or vica versa.<br /> <br /> Anyway, what would your Ascension be?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-05T16:32:35-08:00","id":1528066,"title":"","content":"I think there is evidence for both approaches. I believe that the reason the Free Council has weight in the Supernal is because the symbols of &quot;Human Culture is Magic&quot; had been gaining symbolic weight ever since the Renaissance. The Great Refusal, which involved chasing down traitors and Seers became an Omen for the organization. When the Nameless Alliance was welcomed into the Pentacle by the symbolic leaders of the Diamond and became the Free Council, all the the needed pieces aligned to cause the cosmic &quot;WTF!?&quot; that took the Stewards of the Celestial Orrery off guard (probably the Exarchs too).<br /> <br /> Looking at a Golden Road Ascension, what made Merlin's Ascension genius is that he created the archetype of The Fisher King, which is &quot;The Land and the King are One&quot;, the kingdom reflecting the physical, mental and spiritual state of the ruler. Because it relies on the land being overseen by a great leader (the Prophet's domain), since the monarch's fall brings about its destruction (the specialty of the Ruin) and because it relies on the divine right to rule over an area (which all Exarchs oversee), they could not act against it without diminishing their own personal power. But simultaneously, leaving it be was still a major win for humanity. There was no solution in which the Exarchs didn't end up losing something, which is why the Ruin and Prophet threw Camelot into a uchronia out of sheer spite.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-05T17:56:40-08:00","id":1528071,"title":"","content":"I think the Archmastery/Imperial Magic Ascension is far more reliable, but actually getting to Archmastery is unreliable, so if unreliable is the standard, we can just look at the much less likely to get the attention of the Exarchs, non-Imperial examples/rumours...<br /> <br /> I like the idea of finding/making the perfect DMT which resonates with your Nimbus, a small part of the fallen world which first perfectly into your personal magical archetype - that this would be the first step of a great work which ends in Ascension.<br /> <br /> Kinda like a Promethean's pilgrimage, now that I think about it, but each journey is personal and nothing is guaranteed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-06T07:35:17-08:00","id":1528106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1528028-ascension?p=1528066#post1528066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think there is evidence for both approaches. I believe that the reason the Free Council has weight in the Supernal is because the symbols of &quot;Human Culture is Magic&quot; had been gaining symbolic weight ever since the Renaissance.</div> </div> </div> </div>To The Strongest implies that an attitude of &quot;human works contain magical secrets&quot; could have been applicable as early as 2300 years ago, and simply lacked the political and philosophical premise to be unified under. I don't think anything about whichever of several eras across several parts of the world get the term &quot;Renaissance&quot; applied to them are necessarily significant enough to imply a Supernal transformation by themselves.<br /> <br /> Personally, I've found myself thinking that the model for Ascension given in Imperial Mysteries is a poor fit for the presentation of Second Edition. In particular, I think it weakens the presence and significance of archmasters to have them focus on things in terms of acquiring a certain path to Ascension, as opposed to framing them in terms of their Obsessions and the kinds of Mysteries they have the capability and perspective to pursue. I'd be inclined for an approach to archmasters in which, as far as they know themselves and the lore that trickles down from that to other mages, their types of Obsession do have a tendency to culminate in Ascension, but the process and method is still rather uncertain even among them. From that, while I'd have a sense that most archmasters do have a desire for Ascension, in the absence of any certain way to achieve it much of their deliberate planning and activity is focused towards their Obsessions and the kinds of Mystery they're capable of encountering.<br /> <br /> For other mages, I'd say that studying the nature of how the Supernal and Phenomenal interact and play off of each other, and the process of a mage developing and refining their Supernal selves, do constitute the best way to form a study of how Ascensions happen, they don't ultimately seem to provide a higher incidence of actually achieving it. That dedicated students of Ascension can compile studies of instances where it probably or definitely happened, and plenty of mages who weren't engaged in dedicated Supernal refinement or worldly detachment seem to still manage to achieve that. The conclusion would be that while the idea of what it actually means to Ascend is sound, the actual process of a person becoming a symbol entirely is difficult to pin down in a comprehensive, universally applicable way.<br /> <br /> It goes beyond &quot;there's a sketch of a method of which we can be certain, but is notably difficult for the majority of people to achieve&quot; into &quot;we really need to interrogate and have an open mind towards the question of what it might mean for a person to entirely become a Supernal symbol&quot;. <br /> <br /> Sometimes that might be that a mage's life took on qualities of the archetypal or mythic, but not where they were deliberately trying to play into that. The difference between a person taking the Shadow Name Odin and doing Odin-like things so it can become a Yantra, and people looking back at a person who disappeared and whose last known sighting seems to point to that sarira and thinking &quot;in retrospect, a lot of their life events seem to match up to myths about Odin&quot;. That's not to say that the Ascension would be accidental, but might need to be working on a level other than the conscious, although where active assertions are still needed to overcome the challenges that such a life path creates.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-06T14:10:21-08:00","id":1528124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1528028-ascension?p=1528106#post1528106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The conclusion would be that while the idea of what it actually means to Ascend is sound, the actual process of a person becoming a symbol entirely is difficult to pin down in a comprehensive, universally applicable way.<br /> <br /> It goes beyond &quot;there's a sketch of a method of which we can be certain, but is notably difficult for the majority of people to achieve&quot; into &quot;we really need to interrogate and have an open mind towards the question of what it might mean for a person to entirely become a Supernal symbol&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like to think that a part of 'becoming a Supernal symbol' is making the fallen resonant with a symbol which you already represent.<br /> <br /> Creating the fallen archetype, and a symbol then existing within the Supernal which represents you...<br /> <br /> It could be seen as the purpose of souls, if they are theories to all come from the Supernal and have the capacity to awaken, then it is like they are symbols to being with, passing into the material, altering the Fallen world in a way which manifests themselves, and then becoming part of the Supernal as a result of the experience.<br /> <br /> Like self-writing code. I'd love to mess with some of these ideas in a game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-07T02:28:15-08:00","id":1528146,"title":"","content":"Two other thoughts, long term Nimbus.<br /> <br /> In a way the long term Nimbus as some kind of extension of your Supernal self could be seen as twisting the world toward (or away from) whatever the 'ideal' great work personally synchronizes an individual Mage with the Supernal.<br /> <br /> So studying the specific effects of a long term Nimbus may help understand how that Mage can ascend. On the other hand having their long term Nimbus affect that wrong thing may dilute or confuse the effort.<br /> <br /> Definitely an interesting avenue of exploration (and ingame arguments).<br /> <br /> And secondly, the creation of a legacy.<br /> <br /> It is possible that legacies are the ultimate in bringing the Supernal into the fallen. So this could definitely impact things. Your soul becomes a source of mana specifically keyed to some fallen action (legacy Oblations). Not sure what the use of legacy attainments does (like leaving a Nimbus effect, see above). But I would argue that the most likely result of creating/joining a legacy and binding your soul to that of other mages is the decrease the chances of Ascension.<br /> <br /> The purely personal magical quest is made much more difficult by altering your soul to line up with some many other mages. Maybe it is possible for an entire legacy to ascend at once. Or a legacy which only has one member may be a great work (forging the soul into the perfect fallen reflection of the Supernal?).<br /> <br /> I will have to read a bit more on the theory of legacies... And I suspect some legacy creators (particularly any Liches) are not aiming for Ascension at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-09T13:40:09-08:00","id":1528282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1528028-ascension?p=1528146#post1528146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Two other thoughts, long term Nimbus.<br /> <br /> In a way the long term Nimbus as some kind of extension of your Supernal self could be seen as twisting the world toward (or away from) whatever the 'ideal' great work personally synchronizes an individual Mage with the Supernal.<br /> <br /> So studying the specific effects of a long term Nimbus may help understand how that Mage can ascend. On the other hand having their long term Nimbus affect that wrong thing may dilute or confuse the effort.<br /> <br /> Definitely an interesting avenue of exploration (and ingame arguments).<br /> <br /> And secondly, the creation of a legacy.<br /> <br /> It is possible that legacies are the ultimate in bringing the Supernal into the fallen. So this could definitely impact things. Your soul becomes a source of mana specifically keyed to some fallen action (legacy Oblations). Not sure what the use of legacy attainments does (like leaving a Nimbus effect, see above). But I would argue that the most likely result of creating/joining a legacy and binding your soul to that of other mages is the decrease the chances of Ascension.<br /> <br /> The purely personal magical quest is made much more difficult by altering your soul to line up with some many other mages. Maybe it is possible for an entire legacy to ascend at once. Or a legacy which only has one member may be a great work (forging the soul into the perfect fallen reflection of the Supernal?).<br /> <br /> I will have to read a bit more on the theory of legacies... And I suspect some legacy creators (particularly any Liches) are not aiming for Ascension at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>The True Soul Legacy, found in <i>Grimoire of Grimoires</i> might prove a helpful reference. It was created by a supposedly Atlantean mage, who could not be affected by life extension spells and was not an archmage. The Legacy slowly turns the member into him, with his personality eventually overtaking them. But even if all high level members behave like him and have all his memories, they can be of a different Path than the original and have different skills with the Arcana. Would a member Ascending be the same as the creator Ascending ?<br /> <br /> In my mind, creating or joining a Legacy involves finding a Truth, exploring it and embodying it. An example is the 11th Question saying: &quot;Every question has an answer&quot;, the Uncrowded Kings affirming &quot;manual labor refines the self&quot; or the Sphinxes exclaiming &quot;Some knowledge can only be grasped by an intuitive leap&quot;. I imagine that a mage tricked into joining a Legacy that is not resonant to them will have a harder time Ascending, such as one joining the Echo Walkers before knowing of the soul damage they cause. But otherwise, finding or founding a Legacy with a Truth that is personally important to the mage probably makes Ascending easier.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}